   "id": "math-0013",
   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "**Solution:**\n\nFirst, I find the decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{7} = 0.142857142857142857... = 0.\\overline{142857}$$\n\nThe decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$ has a **repeating period of 6** digits: `142857`.\n\nTo find the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit, I divide 2007 by the period length 6:\n\n$$2007 = 6 \\times 334 + 3$$\n\nSo the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit corresponds to the $3^{\\text{rd}}$ digit in the repeating sequence.\n\nThe repeating sequence is: $1, 4, \\boxed{2}, 8, 5, 7$\n\nTherefore, the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit is **2**.\n\n$$\\boxed{2}$$",
