   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "We need to round $6287215$ to the nearest ten thousand.\n\n**Step 1:** Identify the ten-thousands place.\nThe number is $6287215$.\n- Millions place: $6$\n- Hundred-thousands place: $2$\n- Ten-thousands place: $8$\n- Thousands place: $7$\n- Hundreds place: $2$\n- Tens place: $1$\n- Units place: $5$\n\n**Step 2:** Look at the digit in the thousands place to determine rounding.\nThe thousands digit is $7$, which is $\\geq 5$, so we round up.\n\n**Step 3:** Round up the ten-thousands digit.\nThe ten-thousands digit is $8$, so rounding up gives $9$.\nWe replace all digits to the right of the ten-thousands place with zeros.\n\nSo, $6287215$ rounded to the nearest ten thousand is $6290000$.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Distance to $6280000$: $6287215 - 6280000 = 7215$\n- Distance to $6290000$: $6290000 - 6287215 = 2785$\n- Since $2785 < 7215$, it is closer to $6290000$.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{6290000}$.",
